  "meta": {
    "version": "2026-07-11",
    "title": "Attack-Class Coverage Matrix (machine-readable catalog)",
    "note": "Canonical machine source for tools/enumerate_cells.py + tools/coverage_gate.py + tools/validate_catalog.py. The human-readable companion is coverage-matrix.md; tools/validate_catalog.py asserts the two agree on the class_id set. A class is applicable to a surface unit / listener / asset iff its applies_when predicate is true against that scope's flag set. scope=unit -> one cell per matching surface unit; scope=host -> one cell per distinct listener (host:port); scope=asset -> one cell per asset. negative_kind governs what a genuine-negative (covered_negative) requires: active_probe needs a non-agent tool-log corroborator; reachability needs >= min_vantages distinct verified vantage regions; none accepts a corroborated probe with no extra requirement.",
    "mobile_note": "MAS-* (MASVS-2023) classes cover a mobile APP BUNDLE asset, enumerated from recon/inventory/mobile-surface.json by load_mobile_app(). They are disjoint from the web/API classes by construction: every MAS-* predicate requires the code-derived mobile_app flag, and a mobile asset never acquires http_listener/tls_listener/is_apex/serves_js/has_api, so it enumerates no web class except the unconditional API8-MISCONFIG. The backend API a mobile client talks to is NOT covered by these classes — it is a separate web asset with its own surface.json and the ordinary 24. The optional proof_mode field says what closing the cell as a NEGATIVE requires: static = provable from the artifact, runtime = needs a running device, either = both routes work. coverage_gate.py rejects a deferral whose blocked_on is 'device' on any cell that is not proof_mode:runtime — a missing device cannot excuse work the static route could still do. Deferrals for other blockers (no test tenant, no credentials) are unaffected.",
    "class_count": 39,
    "scope_split": {"unit": 16, "host": 6, "asset": 17},
    "negative_kind_split": {"active_probe": 35, "reachability": 1, "none": 3},
    "key_by_for_scope": {"unit": "unit_id", "host": "listener", "asset": "asset_tag"},
